Committed. Here's what landed:

## The defect

The too young to judge branch of never_forecast_files is a complete no-op in this checkout. Verified: shallow clone, 51 commits, one graft root ~20h old, so git log --diff-filter=A returns that same sha for every path and `shallow_boundary_hides_age` correctly refuses it. Every never-forecast file falls back to the dark set.

CLAUDE.md documented that honestly. What it didn't say is that the consequence is live and steering task selection — this morning's trajectory handed the planner src/format/highlight_lang.rs and src/git_commit_msg.rs as the two darkest rooms. Both were created yesterday as pure moves. Zero bits of information, aimed at my scarcest resource.

## What I built

A first-scored ledger (.yoyo/risk_first_scored.jsonl) — one line per path, once ever, recording when I first scored it. That's a fact about my own observation history, so a graft boundary can't erase it.

• Writer wired inside `write_risk_snapshot_to, the single function every snapshot line passes through, so all three entry points inherit it (/commit, YOYO_RISK_AUTOSNAPSHOT=1 REPL exit, yoyo risk snapshot). Records the whole scored universe, not top_10`. Failure is dropped — the snapshot still lands.
• The founding-batch rule is load-bearing: the first write stamps every currently-scored path at the same instant, so "in the founding batch" means at least as old as the record → None, not a birthday. Reading it as a birthday would have emptied the dark set entirely.
• Consumer in the same diff: handle_risk_epistemic's added_ts closure tries the ledger, falls back to git. never_forecast_files' signature untouched.

## Proof it's forward-only

diff /tmp/before.txt /tmp/after.txt → byte-identical. The ledger doesn't exist yet, so nothing reclassified. It discriminates nothing today and starts paying off around the fifth snapshot. The shallow-clone limitation isn't gone — this routes around it.

8 new tests including the near-miss (a founding-batch path must not be called young) and unparseable-line counting. Module-size register: 3 warnings paid off, including the +3 my own change caused. Gate re-run clean.
